.TH SINKD-SRV 1
.SH NAME
sinkd-srv \- sinkd hub. Stores the files and stays in the foreground.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sinkd-srv
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B sinkd-srv stop
.br
.B sinkd-srv reload
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sinkd-srv
is the hub. It stores every synced file under
.I ~/sinkd-data
unless
.B \-\-sync-root
says otherwise, and it listens on every interface.
When a client runs
.BR sinkd\ pair ,
this process prints a 6-digit code on stderr. Under systemd that is the journal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Use this config file instead of the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-state-dir " path"
Hub state. Default
.IR ~/.local/state/sinkd-srv .
.TP
.BI \-\-runtime-dir " path"
Directory for the control socket. Default
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
.TP
.BI \-\-sync-root " path"
Where synced files are stored. Default
.IR ~/sinkd-data .
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " addr"
Address to listen on. Default
.IR 0.0.0.0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-zenoh-port " port"
Control port. Default 7447.
.TP
.BI \-\-data-port " port"
File-data port. Default 7448.
.TP
.BI \-\-pair-port " port"
Pairing port. Default 7449.
.TP
.BI \-\-pair-code " code"
Fixed pair code, for scripts. Leave unset and the server prints a random code.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B stop
Ask the running hub to exit.
.TP
.B reload
Reload the peer list from state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sinkd/server.toml
Optional bind address, ports, and sync root. Flags override the file.
.TP
.I ~/sinkd-data/
The store. A personal tree lives under a directory for that user. A share lives under
.IR share/ .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sinkd-srv/
Hub keys and peer state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sinkd (1)
